  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1126 AM MDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nHigh pressure remains centered across the area today though it\nwill flatten some over the coming days. As expected, a few more\nclouds are moving across the area due to an uptick in moisture \nand weak waves also moving around the high pressure. Both the\nHRRR and NAMNEST are indicating some very isolated convection\nthis afternoon and evening, mainly over the higher terrain.\nSub-cloud layers remain very dry so don't expect much, if any\nprecip, to hit the ground. This will keep gusty outflow winds\nthe main concern. This trend of afternoon and evening convection\ncontinues into next week. An uptick is progged to occur\nWednesday onwards as a trough approaches from the west and\nallows deeper moisture to start moving into the region. Pair\nthis with several shortwaves moving through and an uptick in\nconvection looks more and more probable. We will likely see a\nreturn to more widespread showers and storms but this far out\nthere is still some model discrepancies. Stay tuned...\n\nTemperatures will remain well above normal for this time of year\nso the going Heat Advisories will remain in place today and\nagain tomorrow. Increased cloud cover during the week will allow\ntemperatures to drop a few degrees so do not expect any products\nduring that timeframe.",
